{
  "version": 1,
  "task": "Execute M0 (Trust-boundary patch / 0.3.1) from .omc/plans/production-hardening-review.md — close live security gaps in @verse8/verse8-mcp before any structural refactor.",
  "scope": "M0 only (7 stories). M1a/M2/M1b/M3/M4 are out of scope; future ralph runs.",
  "constraints": [
    "verse8-mcp is not a standalone git repo in this workspace; do not run git commands. Commits/smoke tests left to the user.",
    "Verification is unit-test based (npm run test:unit) plus tsc and lsp_diagnostics; no git-dependent smoke tests in this ralph run.",
    "All 11 invariants in .omc/ARCHITECTURE.md §5 must remain intact."
  ],
  "stories": [
    {
      "id": "US-M0-1",
      "title": "Add util/redact.ts central redactor + self-test (12 cases) + fuzz seed",
      "priority": 1,
      "passes": true,
      "files": ["src/util/redact.ts (new)", "tests/unit/redact.test.mjs (new)"],
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "src/util/redact.ts exists and exports `safeHint(s: string): string`, `safeErrorHint(e: unknown): string`, and a `SECRET_SHAPES` registry array.",
        "safeHint replaces `glpat-[A-Za-z0-9_-]+` with `glpat-***` in any string.",
        "safeHint replaces `Bearer [A-Za-z0-9._~+/=-]+` with `Bearer [REDACTED]` in any string.",
        "safeHint scrubs `oauth2:[^@\\s]+@` to `oauth2:***@` (covers PATs embedded in clone URLs).",
        "safeHint scrubs JSON `\"access_token\":\"...\"` → `\"access_token\":\"[REDACTED]\"` and same for token / refresh_token.",
        "safeHint is idempotent: safeHint(safeHint(x)) === safeHint(x) for all known shapes.",
        "safeErrorHint accepts unknown (Error, string, undefined, null) and never throws; returns redacted message.",
        "tests/unit/redact.test.mjs has at least 10 cases covering each shape (PAT, Bearer, oauth2, access_token, multi-line, double-redaction, idempotency, non-Error input, undefined, null, no-op safe string, length safety).",
        "All redact tests pass via `node --test tests/unit/redact.test.mjs` against dist/.",
        "tsc compiles src/util/redact.ts cleanly (no errors)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "US-M0-2",
      "title": "Wire MCP dispatch envelopes through safeErrorHint (closes server.ts:278 envelope leak)",
      "priority": 2,
      "passes": true,
      "files": ["src/server.ts", "tests/unit/dispatchRedaction.test.mjs (new)"],
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "src/server.ts CallToolRequestSchema generic catch (currently lines 278–286) wraps `(e as Error).message` via `safeErrorHint(e)` from util/redact.",
        "src/server.ts ReadResourceRequestSchema error path (around line 367) routes its hint through safeErrorHint or safeHint.",
        "src/server.ts GetPromptRequestSchema error path (around line 416) routes its hint through safeErrorHint.",
        "tests/unit/dispatchRedaction.test.mjs constructs a CallTool / ReadResource / GetPrompt request whose handler throws an exception containing every secret shape from SECRET_SHAPES; asserts the JSON-RPC response body contains zero matches via the same regex set.",
        "dispatchRedaction.test has at least 6 cases (3 dispatch surfaces × 2 secret shapes minimum).",
        "All dispatchRedaction tests pass against dist/.",
        "tsc compiles src/server.ts cleanly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "US-M0-3",
      "title": "Migrate existing local redactToken usages to util/redact.ts (deletion-first)",
      "priority": 3,
      "passes": true,
      "files": ["src/tools/newProject.ts", "src/api/agent8Backend.ts"],
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "src/tools/newProject.ts no longer defines a local `redactToken` function (line ~507 removed); call sites import safeHint from util/redact.",
        "src/api/agent8Backend.ts no longer has its inline `truncate()`-with-glpat-redaction (line ~361) — uses safeHint via util/redact instead.",
        "grep `function redactToken|glpat-\\[A-Za-z0-9` returns hits ONLY inside src/util/redact.ts and tests/.",
        "tsc compiles cleanly.",
        "Existing newProjectConfirm.test.mjs passes unchanged (no behavior regression on confirm flow)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "US-M0-4",
      "title": "Add zod schema refinement rejecting projectDir/targetDir path-traversal at MCP dispatch boundary",
      "priority": 4,
      "passes": true,
      "files": ["src/util/safePath.ts (new)", "src/tools/attach.ts", "src/tools/checkpoint.ts", "src/tools/preview.ts", "src/tools/newProject.ts", "tests/unit/safePath.test.mjs (new)"],
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "src/util/safePath.ts exists and exports `isSafeAbsPath(p: string): boolean` and `safeAbsPathSchema(): ZodType<string>`.",
        "isSafeAbsPath rejects strings containing `..` segments, NUL byte (`\\0`), or whose normalization differs from the input (catches `/tmp/../etc`).",
        "isSafeAbsPath accepts plain absolute paths like `/tmp/foo`, `/Users/user/projects/proj`.",
        "isSafeAbsPath accepts `~`-prefixed paths (caller may expand later).",
        "attachInputSchema.projectDir, checkpointInputSchema.projectDir, previewInputSchema.projectDir, newProjectConfirmInputSchema.targetDir each apply the safeAbsPath refinement.",
        "Calling runAttach({projectDir: '../../etc'}) returns structured rejection (zod throws caught at server.ts dispatch and surfaces as tool_exception with the safeErrorHint-wrapped message) BEFORE reaching path.resolve.",
        "tests/unit/safePath.test.mjs has at least 10 cases: `..`-segment, NUL byte, embedded `../`, deeply-nested `..`, valid abs path, valid `~` path, empty string, single dot, `/`, double slash.",
        "All safePath tests pass.",
        "tsc compiles cleanly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "US-M0-5",
      "title": "Pre-clone parent symlink rejection in runNewProjectConfirm",
      "priority": 5,
      "passes": true,
      "files": ["src/tools/newProject.ts"],
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "runNewProjectConfirm checks each segment of the resolved `parentDir` via `fs.lstatSync` BEFORE invoking `git clone`.",
        "When a non-final segment of parentDir is a symlink (and is not `/private/tmp`-style macOS canonical equivalent), the function returns `{ok:false, error:'invalid_parent', hint:<safeHint>}` without spawning git.",
        "macOS `/tmp` symlink to `/private/tmp` is allowed: detection uses `fs.realpathSync` and re-validates the resolved path for `..` traversal so legitimate /tmp use cases pass.",
        "newProjectConfirm.test.mjs adds at least 2 new cases: one with a symlinked parent rejected, one with /tmp accepted.",
        "All newProjectConfirm tests pass.",
        "tsc compiles cleanly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "US-M0-6",
      "title": "Replace inline Bearer redaction in proxy/imageMcp.ts with util/redact.ts",
      "priority": 6,
      "passes": true,
      "files": ["src/proxy/imageMcp.ts"],
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "src/proxy/imageMcp.ts no longer has the inline `replace(/Bearer\\s+[A-Za-z0-9._~+/=-]+/gi, ...)` regex (around line 366); uses safeHint from util/redact instead.",
        "grep `Bearer\\\\s\\+` in src/ returns matches ONLY inside src/util/redact.ts.",
        "tsc compiles cleanly.",
        "Existing tests for proxy/imageMcp pass unchanged."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "US-M0-7",
      "title": "Token file permission warning on read",
      "priority": 7,
      "passes": true,
      "files": ["src/context/token.ts"],
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "src/context/token.ts loadToken() warns to stderr when the resolved token file's mode is not exactly 0600 (`stat.mode & 0o777 !== 0o600`).",
        "Warning never refuses to read the token (backwards compat — only warns).",
        "Warning is rate-limited to once per process per file path (avoid spamming on every loadToken call).",
        "If the platform is Windows (process.platform === 'win32'), the check is skipped (no POSIX modes there).",
        "Existing token.ts callers are unaffected (no signature change).",
        "tsc compiles cleanly."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "verification": {
    "gates": [
      "All M0 ACs verified by reviewer (oh-my-claudecode:architect default)",
      "tsc compiles entire src/ cleanly",
      "node --test tests/unit/*.test.mjs runs all tests including new ones — 100% pass",
      "lsp_diagnostics returns 0 errors on every file changed in this run",
      "Mandatory deslop pass on changed files (oh-my-claudecode:ai-slop-cleaner)",
      "Post-deslop regression re-run passes (npm run build && node --test tests/unit/*.test.mjs)"
    ]
  },
  "out_of_scope_for_this_ralph": [
    "Smoke tests (require git operations / mock servers — verified separately by user)",
    "Live e2e tests against prod (manual)",
    "M1a, M2, M1b, M3, M4 milestones (future ralph runs)",
